WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.269
Here on New Call, an authorized dispatcher is preparing

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.920
a fictional community standby.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:09.850
The Name identifies it as training, and Nature explains the exercise.

00:00:10.239 --> 00:00:13.149
Priority is Routine and Type is Medical.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.899
Use a clear description and the choices that fit your department.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.290
These details help the next dispatcher understand the scheduled work without

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.569
treating this example as a real incident.

00:00:23.709 --> 00:00:28.120
In Select Dispatch Recipients, Wallace Boden is the one checked person.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.209
Everyone is unchecked, and the footer confirms one selected.

00:00:32.659 --> 00:00:35.980
Check both the name and the count before choosing Confirm.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.739
This training account has No location, so this selection does not demonstrate

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:42.380
a nearest-person calculation.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:46.100
The point here is to keep the planned dispatch list specific.

00:00:46.269 --> 00:00:50.850
The prepared Scheduled Date and Time is October thirty-first, twenty twenty-six,

00:00:50.959 --> 00:00:53.029
at eight in the morning on this device.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:56.189
Dispatch To still shows one selected.

00:00:56.719 --> 00:01:00.130
When entering a new schedule, choose a time at least fifteen

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:03.959
minutes ahead; Dispatch checks that lead time when creating the call.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:09.539
Before using Create, check the date, the time and the intended recipients together.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.500
Leave Save as pending off for this scheduled-call exercise.

00:01:13.919 --> 00:01:18.279
Its explanation describes a different choice: a pending call is saved and

00:01:18.279 --> 00:01:22.510
numbered, with the proposed recipients retained, while nobody is notified

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:24.319
and the field apps do not see it.

00:01:24.739 --> 00:01:28.680
Here, with the future date set and the pending option off, choose

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.799
Create to save the scheduled call.

00:01:31.019 --> 00:01:35.490
The scheduled-call list now shows the saved entry with Medical, Routine

00:01:35.599 --> 00:01:39.380
and a Scheduled For time of October thirty-first at ten in the morning.

00:01:39.829 --> 00:01:43.149
The narrow columns shorten the call number and name on this screen.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:46.960
Open the row to read the complete identity and confirm the saved

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.220
schedule before making further changes.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.470
Call Details shows the complete call number and the training standby name.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:58.630
The blue Scheduled for banner and the Info date row both show ten in the morning.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.599
Read the saved result here.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:04.509
An entry remaining on this screen with a future schedule is not

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:08.589
evidence that recipients have already received or acknowledged a dispatch.

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:11.140
Look again at the prepared eight o’clock value.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.660
This picker uses the device clock.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:17.060
The saved call shows ten o’clock in the department clock.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.220
That two-hour difference here represents the same scheduled instant.

00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:24.730
Read the saved date and time with your team before relying on the

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:29.129
schedule, especially when dispatchers use devices in different time zones.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:33.190
To move this planned dispatch, use Edit on Call Details.

00:02:33.589 --> 00:02:36.260
This walkthrough follows the full Edit Call form.

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:40.429
Keep the same call identity so the revised schedule remains attached

00:02:40.429 --> 00:02:42.139
to the original training standby.

00:02:42.429 --> 00:02:46.519
In the Scheduled Date and Time picker, October thirty-first is selected.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:50.400
The Hour column shows nine, and the Minute column shows thirty.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:54.719
Set the intended date and time in these controls, then choose Done.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:59.469
That commits the picker value to the edit form; it has not saved the call yet.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:03.359
The Edit Call form now shows October thirty-first at nine thirty

00:03:03.359 --> 00:03:04.960
in the morning on this device.

00:03:05.339 --> 00:03:10.049
Check that replacement value, and confirm that Dispatch To still has one selected.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:13.990
A changed schedule must also be at least fifteen minutes ahead.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:18.210
The helper explains that leaving this field empty keeps the current schedule;

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.850
it does not remove the scheduled dispatch.

00:03:20.999 --> 00:03:24.719
At the bottom of Edit Call, choose Save to submit the change.

00:03:25.119 --> 00:03:28.269
Review the result on the call itself before telling anyone

00:03:28.269 --> 00:03:29.560
that its schedule has moved.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.999
The selected value in the editor was preparation; the

00:03:32.999 --> 00:03:34.399
saved call is the readback.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:38.290
Call updated successfully appears on the same training call.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:42.809
The Scheduled for banner and Info row now show eleven thirty in the

00:03:42.809 --> 00:03:44.430
morning in the department clock.

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:48.130
That is the saved result of choosing nine thirty on this device.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.010
The call is still scheduled.

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:55.150
Use this pattern for a fire or EMS standby, a community paramedicine

00:03:55.199 --> 00:03:58.500
or mental-health coordination exercise, a search-and-rescue

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:03.160
briefing, planned security support, a wildland contractor drill, or

00:04:03.189 --> 00:04:04.959
industrial response-team training.

00:04:05.369 --> 00:04:09.289
Agree on the event time, select the intended recipients, save

00:04:09.289 --> 00:04:12.330
the schedule, and read back the department time on the call.
